# Figure outputs (PDFs directly under Plots/, SVGs under Plots/SVG/). The notebooks
# regenerate every one of them and are themselves the record of what was produced
# (their saved cell outputs), so none of this is versioned: a partial, partly stale
# set on disk is worse than none (an old Fig6.pdf from a RUN_TAG="plain" run once sat
# here looking like the published figure). Every notebook that writes here creates
# the directory itself on first run (end of its imports cell), so no .gitkeep is
# needed. The two pickled sweep summaries Figure4.ipynb reads as INPUT
# live in Plots_data/ instead, not here, since they are not regenerable output.
Plots/

# The snapshot tree. Held back from git deliberately: it ships as a GitHub release
# asset (see datasets/README.md), so the repository stays cloneable without it.
# Its layout and per-file digests stay tracked, so a copy can always be verified.
datasets/*
!datasets/README.md
!datasets/MANIFEST.sha256
.vscode/
.claude/

# The trained runs behind the figures. Same treatment as datasets/ above: held back
# from git and shipped as a GitHub release asset (see Plots_data/README.md), so the
# repository stays light. Layout and per-file digests stay tracked via the manifest.
# App_I_data/README.md documents SR provenance and is kept tracked too; the other
# App_*_data subfolders carry no README of their own. The two pickled LBC summaries
# are Figure4.ipynb's actual input data, not regenerable output, so they stay
# tracked as well (see Plots_data/README.md).
Plots_data/*
!Plots_data/README.md
!Plots_data/MANIFEST.sha256
!Plots_data/results_LBC_Lambdamax_Ising_summary.pkl
!Plots_data/results_LBC_Lambdamax_XY_XZ_summary_new.pkl
!Plots_data/App_I_data/
Plots_data/App_I_data/*
!Plots_data/App_I_data/README.md

# activation caches written by Figure6_boundary_fit_comparison.ipynb
.cache_*.npz

# Zipped datasets/ and Plots_data/, staged here locally for upload to a GitHub
# release. Not part of the repository itself.
/release_assets/
